 * die() means the sync itself failed (the workflow step fails); a completed
 * run with zero Zephyr-tagged tests is a normal pass, not an error.
 *
 * Why this exists instead of BrowserStack's native Zephyr integration: that
 * integration's setup flow only accepts a Jira host, with no field for a
 * custom Zephyr API base URL — and this org's Zephyr Scale instance is
 * DE-hosted (https://de.api.zephyrscale.smartbear.com), not one of
 * BrowserStack's supported regions. See .docs/temp/SFCC-751-implementation-spec.md.
 *
 * Zephyr key mapping: reads each BrowserStack test result's `tags` array for
 * a `@zephyr:<KEY>` tag (confirmed via BrowserStack's Get Tests API to carry
